{"chunk_id":"R1-2504779-002","collection":"ran1_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Samsung"],"tdocNumber":"R1-2504779","title":"Summary of discussion on HARQ-ACK aspects of Rel-17 multi-PDSCH scheduling"},"point_id":"6184799579383354177"}
In [1], Samsung discussed an issue on Type-2 HARQ-ACK codebook when a UE indicates the UE capability “type2-HARQ-ACK-Codebook” (FG 18-9) and multi-PDSCH scheduling is configured. The corresponding draft CR was also submitted in [2]. In particular, the UE behavior for FG 18-9 is shown below. If the current Rel-17 specifications, as per Excerpt #1, is directly applied to Rel-17 multi-PDSCH scheduling, the UE needs to count (and run the pseudo-code for) a corresponding serving cell based on the number of scheduled PDSCHs, . Such counting would be against the DAI principle agreed in Rel-17 multi-PDSCH scheduling, that DAI counting is per DCI format, and not per scheduled PDSCH. To address this issue, Samsung proposed to count (and run the pseudo-code for) a corresponding serving cell based on the number of DCI formats and not the number of scheduled PDSCH receptions. The following proposal is proposed in [1] and the corresponding CR is presented in [2]. Proposal from [1]: Clarify that, when a UE receives multiple DCI formats in a same PDCCH MO, and at least one of the DCI formats schedules multiple PDSCHs on a same serving cell, the UE counts (and runs the Type-2 HARQ-ACK pseudo-code for) the serving cell a same number of times as the number of DCI formats and not the number of scheduled PDSCH receptions. Q1: Do you agree with the proposal from [1]? Q2: Do you agree with the draft CR proposed from [2]? Q3: Any other comments? TBD

